ss occurs when a greater portion of probability is assigned to unfavorable outcomes. Since both outcomes have 50%, no lottery is more right-skewed. Therefore, the reason cannot clearly prefer one over the other based on skewness. Nonetheless, the reason can be applied in principle to the decision problem, as skewness is a property that can be assessed from the outcomes and probabilities.",
